**Definition 108.3 (the paid repair images).** For $d=0$ fix one of the
two readout templates in Theorem 107.1. At its completed odd endpoint,
use the following *different* Time and supplemented Boundary:

| Expression | Content at the performed repair endpoint |
| --- | --- |
| Space | Actual grown graph/law and $BH\theta$ |
| Time | Actual constructor causal order and this finite late repair window, including its real Tick/Hold, selected terminal labels, epochs, literal replies and complete returns |
| Boundary-plus | Earned ordered terminal metric and current designated germ, together with those $k$ actually acquired terminal samples at their recorded repair epoch |
| Memory | The newly installed full current predictor and genuine callable context |

Boundary-plus is a sampled boundary trace supplemented by a past paid
window, not a renamed claim that the current designated germ changed.
It is identically zero only in its germ component. For $d>0$ the analogous
repair views include the actually retained literal $s_0=R\theta$ in the
Time/Boundary-plus record, explicitly as prior retained data, plus their
$k-d$ performed samples. They do not label the $s_0$ entries as new
measurements. At $d=k$ this is the zero-call retained-data image at
$H\theta$; its Time window has no fictitious Tick or Read.

